{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm","id":1032271,"title":"Managing Paradigm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-15T12:50:33-08:00","id":1032271,"title":"Managing Paradigm","content":"One of the discussions in the Vampire forums has drifted over into Mage territory, so I thought I would ask the people of the Mage forum to contribute to the discussion through a separate thread. We are discussing the importance of Paradigm and how much STs should use Paradigms to focus the abilities of Mage characters within their chronicles. My perspective is that Mages cannot use True Magick to do anything outside of the limitations of their Paradigms because their Paradigms are what allow them to create effects of True Magick. Could you share your perspective on the importance of Paradigms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T13:01:49-08:00","id":1032285,"title":"","content":"Paradigm makes magic. Without paradigm there is no basis for the mage to focus their belief.<br /> You can't do lay-on hands healing if you don't believe there's a God or other Deity who is channelling their power through you.<br /> You can't do blood magic unless you believe there is magical energy in blood.<br /> You can't hack the world unless you think the world has a code to hack.<br /> You can't make all sound disappear by creating a vacuum unless you believe sound cannot travel in a vacuum.<br /> <br /> Without paradigm, there is no magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T13:07:16-08:00","id":1032289,"title":"","content":"What Saukou said.<br /> <br /> Now, the process of gaining Arete - increasing your enlightenment and moving past your limitations - is the process of broadening your paradigm, changing your paradigm, completely switching them to a different paradigm, or even the opposite - becoming more focused, obsessive and steadfast in the one you current have. Either way, it is a change, a spiritual and mental growth in the mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T13:35:08-08:00","id":1032302,"title":"","content":"Well, my understanding it's the same. A mage needs its Paradigm. M20 goes so far as to say that mages can surpass the need to use their Instruments/Foci with time and Arete, but that they never surpass their Paradigm.<br /> <br /> Then again, some paragraphs disagree, as there are situations in wich a mage can do stuff without believing strongly in what he's doing (it's +2 to difficulty and vulgar with witnesses). The rare defect Sleepwalker permits the creation of a mage character that doesn't believe in his own magick (or in any magick). Stuff happens when she realy wants to, but the very mage count as witness. But the spirit of the rules seems to be that, in general, a mage needs to believe in what he's doing to do something.<br /> It says &quot;the fact that you don't believe that god wil send angels to help you, doesn't mean that you can't pray for it to happen&quot;. That's how Sleepwalkers do their stuff.<br /> However, this implies that the mage believes...otherwise, why pray instead of meditate, cry for help, or do some stuff appropiate to a non christian religion. I can't pray if I don't know the superstitions arround that gesture. In a sense, Sleepwalker doesn't mean that the mage &quot;doesn't believe&quot;, but rather that has a weak belief. The kind of beliefs you have latent for your culture. Not enough to &quot;properly&quot; shape reality, but the Avatar can work with it.<br /> In M20 there are rules for grabing the focus of other mage and use it despite your Paradigm (+2 to the difficulty, for unfamiliar tools, and it's Vulgar with Witnesses). Like if you were Sleepwalking, but voluntarily. Which it's something I abhor, and goes contrary to any Mage book ever written, but it's there.<br /> <br /> There are instances where magick can be cast unconsciously. This it's called Wild Magick, and, obviously, isn't limmited by Paradigm. It has it's own rules, and is very rare. Usually it happens in the Awakening of the mage, before Paradigm &quot;sets in&quot;. <hr /><br /> A mage can do anything, but only with great effort, this effort coalesce in the Focus/Paradigm.<br /> In other words, a mage's magick IT'S is Paradigm. The fact that the curses, magick words, and all other stuff works it's construed by the &quot;reality warping&quot; of the mage in action, changing the rules so that they adapt to the Paradigm. That's why, in a sense, everything that the mage does it's magical. That's why it's said that Mages ARE magick. They don't &quot;do magick&quot;, they live it.<br /> <br /> This doesn't mean that Mages live in permanent solipsism. They have strong beliefs, but these can be contested, expanded, and even broken. In these situations, the magick of the mage changes. A mage can learn from other Paradigms, expanding his own to addapt to the new data. A mage can have a crisis of faith, or convert to other Paradigm. In this case, I see the use of the rules for Sleepwalkers, until the mage can solidify her Paradigm, but I don't see magick outside ANY Paradigm. Even the Sleepwalker needs to pray, after all.<br /> Neither I see this &quot;movement of the mind&quot; (the one necessary to do stuff outside your Paradigm), as something that can be done casualy. That is, outside a crisis of faith or something equaly deep. Albeit M20 disagrees on this (paradoxicaly, if we take in that they went out of their way to deny that a mage can ever surpass his Paradigm).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-15-2017, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T16:39:04-08:00","id":1032376,"title":"","content":"I largely agree with Aleph here. And the sleepwalker thing coincides with the 'spontanious effects' rule of Technocrats. Where they're not CREATING The effect, they in their desperation are looking for something to save themselves and <i>notice</i> something. Like that the roof is weakening. Or the boiler is about to explode. They believe that yes, that's possible and it would totally save their ass, but they 'know' they didn't cause it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T20:12:43-08:00","id":1032446,"title":"","content":"At our game table paradigm is everything. It doesn't matter what the spheres allow you to do if your belief of magic doesn't support it it can't be done by you. Furthermore if you can't tell me how you do it through your focus you can't do it either. However I'm helpful in this area as much as is needed, especially with new players. Paradigm is what the game is about, it can't be ignore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T23:52:10-08:00","id":1032517,"title":"","content":"For all the talk of how &quot;paradigm is everything,&quot; in application paradigm is largely window dressing. Cases were paradigm actually hard restricts a mage's capabilities are rare edge cases at worst.<br /> <br /> Paradigms are how a mage sees magic in a very big picture way. Most mages can't just lay their hands on you and pray until you're miraculously healed in a brief moment. The vast majority of mages have some in-paradigm method framed by their practice(s) and instruments to use Life 3 to heal someone.<br /> <br /> The &quot;limitations of paradigm,&quot; are generally vastly overblown in terms of practical application to game-play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T03:04:31-08:00","id":1032566,"title":"","content":"I agree to a certain degree with the most common statements here, and of course with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> observations, but I want to add something.<br /> <br /> The game is about Paradigm, but not only this. It is about transcendence, including transcendence from one's own Paradigm. OoC this is represented through shedding Instruments/Foci as one ascends in the Arete ladder. IC this is further represented through a number of characters that, being or not able to make use of this, just grasped the truth: that magic comes from Will, not Belief.<br /> <br /> At the end, the game offer simple rules for anyone, at any level, to just ignore Paradigm and do shit. At the end of the day, the power comes from the person. But even archmages will follow their Paradigm most of the time, because it is as much their will as the final effects. Belief shifts from being &quot;how I think that the world works&quot; to &quot;how I think that the world <u>should</u> work&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T05:22:24-08:00","id":1032594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1032517#post1032517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For all the talk of how &amp;quot;paradigm is everything,&amp;quot; in application paradigm is largely window dressing. Cases were paradigm actually hard restricts a mage's capabilities are rare edge cases at worst.<br /> <br /> Paradigms are how a mage sees magic in a very big picture way. Most mages can't just lay their hands on you and pray until you're miraculously healed in a brief moment. The vast majority of mages have some in-paradigm method framed by their practice(s) and instruments to use Life 3 to heal someone.<br /> <br /> The &amp;quot;limitations of paradigm,&amp;quot; are generally vastly overblown in terms of practical application to game-play.</div> </div> </div> </div>I usually employ what seems to be an unpopular approach to address this. Unpopular in that each time I suggest it, it gets challenged as unfair. <br /> <br /> I have the mages paradigm dictate what counts as under the preview of their spheres.<br /> Forces 2 can move darkness or photons, to change dark into light is Forces 3, but moving photons around is just Forces 2.<br /> <br /> If you believe sickness is a spirit sucking the energy from you, you need spirit along with Life to banish the spirit, or at least commune with it to get it to leave the victim alone. Otherwise, Life is the only way to cure disease.<br /> <br /> If you believe in the multiverse theory, stepping sideways is more likely to take you to Mirror zones, while the shaman is more likely to head towards the middle umbra.<br /> <br /> If you believe in destiny, then any attempt to loop time to change outcomes is going to result in similar, if shifted events without a bit of Entropy to guide it. If you believe things are just random, Time for looping is enough to change events, but without Entropy you'll have problems getting the outcome you desire.<br /> <br /> If you use Corr and are a heavy Tech mage, things like IP addresses, phone numbers, and GPS coordinates will be much more useful to you for finding the target than body samples or important objects, while a heavy mystic mage would not get much out of knowing their targets IP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T06:36:47-08:00","id":1032622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1032517#post1032517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For all the talk of how &amp;quot;paradigm is everything,&amp;quot; in application paradigm is largely window dressing. Cases were paradigm actually hard restricts a mage's capabilities are rare edge cases at worst.<br /> <br /> Paradigms are how a mage sees magic in a very big picture way. Most mages can't just lay their hands on you and pray until you're miraculously healed in a brief moment. The vast majority of mages have some in-paradigm method framed by their practice(s) and instruments to use Life 3 to heal someone.<br /> <br /> The &amp;quot;limitations of paradigm,&amp;quot; are generally vastly overblown in terms of practical application to game-play.</div> </div> </div> </div>In some since this can be very true. Paradigm will far more often simply restrict &quot; how&quot; and effect is done than decide &quot;if&quot; it can be done. The most common difference ultimately being the time it takes and how obvious it appears. <br /> <br /> One example though hardly the only way would be mind shielding. An Akashic could simply meditate for an hour or so to gird his mind's defences for the day. An Etherite on the otherhand might build himself an aluminum hat to wear in order to reflect the mind control powers of aliens. Ya that was to funny to resist. <br /> <br /> Eitherway results in the same outcome as far as the effect goes though one could certainly stand out. Incidentally they probably both take about the same amount of time initially, but afterwards the Etherite has the hat and now he could work the effect fairly quickly whereas the Akashic still needs a few hours of meditation.<br /> <br /> Maybe some game tables use paradigm to a lesser or greater extent than ours. For us it is what the game builds off of. After all the overall premis of Mage is to bring forth your paradigm to consensual reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T07:29:03-08:00","id":1032647,"title":"","content":"I guess I am in the minority because Paradigm is everything in my games. If you cannot explain how an effect functions by the logic of your Paradigm (the player, not the character), you cannot do that effect. If you want to have linear magic, where the Paradigm gives access to effect rather than shaping the effect, then I believe that a Sorcerer is a more thematically appropriate character than a Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T07:36:56-08:00","id":1032652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1032647#post1032647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I am in the minority because Paradigm is everything in my games. If you cannot explain how an effect functions by the logic of your Paradigm (the player, not the character), you cannot do that effect. If you want to have linear magic, where the Paradigm gives access to effect rather than shaping the effect, then I believe that a Sorcerer is a more thematically appropriate character than a Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this; in my games, paradigm is everything. If there is no way to work in your paradigm and rituals, you can't perform the effect at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T09:12:25-08:00","id":1032700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1032647#post1032647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess I am in the minority because Paradigm is everything in my games. If you cannot explain how an effect functions by the logic of your Paradigm (the player, not the character), you cannot do that effect. If you want to have linear magic, where the Paradigm gives access to effect rather than shaping the effect, then I believe that a Sorcerer is a more thematically appropriate character than a Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this and with Manus. Characters can get REALLY creative and try to access parts of the possibilities of their Spheres, but for each Paradigm (old meaning, new meaning as a part of Focus is something completely different) there are things that are easy and things that are going to be difficult. And, when something is difficult, if there is some way to torture the Paradigm into making it happen, it tends to be something pretty complex and difficult and takes time, usually without the extra advantage of getting reduction on Diff.<br /> <br /> Recently this came up in my current game. We have two characters with Mind 3, one in the NWO and the other a Cultist transcendentalist poet from the 19th Century (sorta like Thoreau if he was a wandering mountain man). The party was scattered across a small commune/farm doing their own thing when something came up. The NWO (who is the acknowledged party 'leader' insofar as such a role exists), wanted to set up a telepathic network, linking their minds together in a sort of &quot;party line&quot;. But the questions came up as to how he would do that considering his Focus and the NWO paradigm. He finally just settled on contacting them all by a message to their miniaturized cell phone/bluetooth/ear buds (because the group has a sorta Son of Ether... actually a 1940's era Technocratic Virtual Adept, but he's &quot;getting better&quot;). It was easier to just use actual technology. Later the Cultist wanted to do very much the same thing, but he could. He drew pictures of them in his journal and wrote a sort of call and response poem about a fictive/actual telepathic meeting of the minds they had.... It made the communication a little weird for the participants as what they thought they were saying would echo in their heads as Hank's poetry and what everyone else would hear was that poetic version of their intended communication. But it worked. <br /> <br /> We had the usual &quot;Magely&quot; discussion about the whole situation and it became obvious that there were also things that Douglas, aka Agent Martin, could do that would also be difficult for Hank to pull off.... Like using his Mind 3 (yes, yes, there was also Correspondence involved for all this), he could use the ear buds as a communication medium and use his Mind 3 to completely encode the communication. So they could sound like they were talking about the weather or sports, but Douglas could be dropping words with the right intonation and cadence to convey his actual meaning and, in doing so, actually &quot;clue in&quot; the other participants so they were all &quot;in on&quot; the code and would/could use it back. Hank would have had a much harder time trying to do that, as his Paradigm is all about &quot;Truth&quot; and &quot;Beauty&quot; and &quot;Naturalness&quot; and using words that way is lying and unnatural and therefore ugly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T09:25:16-08:00","id":1032706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1032594#post1032594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I usually employ what seems to be an unpopular approach to address this. Unpopular in that each time I suggest it, it gets challenged as unfair.<br /> <br /> I have the mages paradigm dictate what counts as under the preview of their spheres.<br /> Forces 2 can move darkness or photons, to change dark into light is Forces 3, but moving photons around is just Forces 2.<br /> <br /> If you believe sickness is a spirit sucking the energy from you, you need spirit along with Life to banish the spirit, or at least commune with it to get it to leave the victim alone. Otherwise, Life is the only way to cure disease.<br /> <br /> If you believe in the multiverse theory, stepping sideways is more likely to take you to Mirror zones, while the shaman is more likely to head towards the middle umbra.<br /> <br /> If you believe in destiny, then any attempt to loop time to change outcomes is going to result in similar, if shifted events without a bit of Entropy to guide it. If you believe things are just random, Time for looping is enough to change events, but without Entropy you'll have problems getting the outcome you desire.<br /> <br /> If you use Corr and are a heavy Tech mage, things like IP addresses, phone numbers, and GPS coordinates will be much more useful to you for finding the target than body samples or important objects, while a heavy mystic mage would not get much out of knowing their targets IP.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see much about this I would disagree with or challenge. <br /> <br /> Except that I have serious problems with Entropy as written (as being redundant to the point of uselessness and being designed out of whack with the Sphere system altogether) but everything in that line would fall under Paradigm (not new Focus meaning, old meaning) and Time. But that's a personal thing that doesn't really matter for purposes of this discussion. <br /> <br /> But, really, most sincerely, I have an issue in punishing mages for their Paradigm by forcing Sphere-bloat on them. Why can't the spiritualist just summon a spirit of healing and make the deal and have the spirit do the healing? (Just using Spirit to do it.) Or, why can't the spiritualist have made a prior deal with a spirit of healing that allows them to channel the spirit's power, allowing them to heal without the spirit's presence or direct intervention and possibly in ways that the spirit might not have thought to use that power itself? (Being the reason that the spiritualist has Life in the first place, but, limited to the deals made.... so, to hurt people, another deal would need to be made to use those Life effects or the healing spirit would also have to be a harming spirit and probably thereby more powerful and harder to make the deal with). <br /> <br /> This is the same issue with forcing magical or &quot;scientific&quot; psions to use Mind with every effect because it comes from their minds. Spheres are about EFFECTS, the results intended. The means of making that happen is the CAUSES and those are all about paradigms. If your psionic character is a Firestarter, the mental power is part of the Paradigm and the starting of fires is using the Forces Sphere. (And then there's the issues related to how your character came by/has such powers... An Etherite psionic might need the Bizzaro helmet or the glowing green injection, while the Akashic might need some breathing exercises and the proper mudras....)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T13:30:31-08:00","id":1032879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm#post1032271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the discussions in the Vampire forums has drifted over into Mage territory, so I thought I would ask the people of the Mage forum to contribute to the discussion through a separate thread. We are discussing the importance of Paradigm and how much STs should use Paradigms to focus the abilities of Mage characters within their chronicles. My perspective is that Mages cannot use True Magick to do anything outside of the limitations of their Paradigms because their Paradigms are what allow them to create effects of True Magick. Could you share your perspective on the importance of Paradigms?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just going to quote the Guide to the Traditions here and where it discusses the four different styles of Paradigms:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li><b>Rigid</b>: Mages with a rigid paradigm <i>know</i> that their way is the only true way. What other practice might look like magic, but it is definitely not. Such a mage has to translate every rote or spell from another paradigm than his own into a way that fits his style.</li> <li><b>Closed</b>: A closed paradigm acknowledges that other paradigms might exist, but assumes that they are incomplete or otherwise unfit for magic.</li> <li><b>Open</b>: An open paradigm holds that other paradigms might contain a kernel of truth, but that his personal paradigm works best for him. He has no problem sharing and adapting knowledge from other traditions.</li> <li><b>Liberal</b>: A liberal paradigm holds that everything is true and therefore combines multiple assumptions from various paradigms into a wild mish-mash.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div>Considering that the same book states that Mages with open and liberal paradigms can learn rotes, effects, and styles from other Traditions, I'm not seeing paradigm as the straightjacket you're suggestion.<br /> <br /> If my paradigm as a Celestial Chorister is &quot;God makes His miracles work through me,&quot; then it's really hard to justify why any particular Sphere effect is out of bounds. Unless you're trying to argue that the Chorister would see that God is somehow limited in His actions, and therefore can't generate a cloak of invisibility around the Chorister using Forces 3, or give them the ability to fly like an Angel with Forces 3, or let them call down fire from Heaven with Forces 3...<br /> <br /> ...or become an invisible, flying predator drone while calling down fire from the heavens using multiple Forces 3 effects...<br /> <br /> This is the problem of a liberal paradigm with a vague, yet valid description of &quot;God does it,&quot; if you're trying to use paradigm as a straightjacket instead of a tool to enhance roleplaying. The more liberal the paradigm, the more you can justify using your Spheres to do, and the less incentive you have to play a rigid or closed paradigm. <br /> <br /> Personally, I always prefer to think about the effect I want, then justify it through paradigm. Not think to myself &quot;Would my Akashic monk believe he could fly using Forces?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":1515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","user":"BenjCano","date":". 01-16-2017, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T13:34:43-08:00","id":1032883,"title":"","content":"But that is more of a Marauder Paradigm than a Celestial Choir Paradigm. If their players want unlimited power, then the STs should run medium Quiet Marauder games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T14:04:32-08:00","id":1032902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1032883#post1032883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that is more of a Marauder Paradigm than a Celestial Choir Paradigm. If their players want unlimited power, then the STs should run medium Quiet Marauder games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you're trying to argue that religious belief is insanity (I don't think you are but I'm stating that as my premise just to put it out there) I don't see why &quot;God is all powerful and can do anything and manifests His miracles through me if I say my prayers&quot; would make a Mage a Marauder and not a Chorister.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T14:22:05-08:00","id":1032911,"title":"","content":"And this is why M20 redefined how paradigm interacts with things: to have something that ensures (non-Marauder) mages are operating on a consistent set of believes without the silliness that comes from the &quot;straight jacket&quot; approach many STs and Internet debaters developed over the years to resist the silliness of excesses of white-room creative approaches to paradigm.<br /> <br /> To paraphrase both 2e and Revised on this, paradigm is meant to <b>inform</b> how your role-play your mage, not turn into a philosophic argument or metaphysical treatise every time you cast a spell. This is a game meant to be played for fun. Paradigm is there to help players frame their role-playing to make for a consistent and fun magical praxis in a very loose and open system, not to be a cudgel for STs to smack players with. Yes, sometimes the ST needs to step in, but the books have been spending over 20 years encouraging us to resist that urge unless absolutely necessary.<br /> <br /> By the time you're actually playing the game, &quot;how does this fit your paradigm?&quot; should be a rare question. 99% of the time mages will use their tools and practices as informed by their paradigm which means that answer is front loaded in. If prayer is a significant part of a mage's technique as defined through there paradigm, then when they kneel in front of a shrine to pray to [insert devotional entity] they've already said how this fits into their paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T15:40:48-08:00","id":1032959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1032902#post1032902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless you're trying to argue that religious belief is insanity (I don't think you are but I'm stating that as my premise just to put it out there) I don't see why &quot;God is all powerful and can do anything and manifests His miracles through me if I say my prayers&quot; would make a Mage a Marauder and not a Chorister.</div> </div> </div> </div>'God has given me ultimate power and the right to do whatever I want' is a common delusion among the white jacket crowd so it fits well within the Marauder paradigm. Religion is supposed to be about humility, not temporal power, so a more proper viewpoint for a Chorister would be 'I surrender my will to God so that God may do His (or Her) will through my unworthy hands'. 'God is all powerful and can do anything and manifests His miracles through me if I say my prayers' might as well be 'I tell the Old Fart in the Clouds what to do and He had better do what I want if He knows what is best for Him' because that is effective what the player is doing if the ST does not require the player to actually roleplay the Paradigm that the player chose for their Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T15:53:03-08:00","id":1032964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1032959#post1032959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'God has given me ultimate power and the right to do whatever I want' is a common delusion among the white jacket crowd so it fits well within the Marauder paradigm. Religion is supposed to be about humility, not temporal power, so a more proper viewpoint for a Chorister would be 'I surrender my will to God so that God may do His (or Her) will through my unworthy hands'. 'God is all powerful and can do anything and manifests His miracles through me if I say my prayers' might as well be 'I tell the Old Fart in the Clouds what to do and He had better do what I want if He knows what is best for Him' because that is effective what the player is doing if the ST does not require the player to actually roleplay the Paradigm that the player chose for their Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Name an effect you think should be inappropriate for a Chorister to produce with, say, Forces 3 by praying for it. &quot;Our Father, who art in Heaven. Please bestow Your power upon me by X...&quot;<br /> <br /> What, in your estimation, is an inappropriate value of X for a Forces effect up to level 3?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:24:37-08:00","id":1033027,"title":"","content":"Every one of them. A more appropriate prayer is something like 'Oh Father, who art in Heaven, please spare these innocents from X'. The exact effect is suggested by the player and, if it fits within their Paradigm and within their Spheres, the ST approves the effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:26:59-08:00","id":1033031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1032959#post1032959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'God has given me ultimate power and the right to do whatever I want' is a common delusion among the white jacket crowd...</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't matter if delusional people believe this. There are non-delusional people that believe it as well.<br /> <br /> In addition to this, being insane or crazy is not the same as being a Marauder. Lots of non-Marauder mages would be considered 'crazy' by normal people. The mental trauma of awakening makes psychological Flaws fairly easy to justify for mages without forcing them into being Marauders.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...so it fits well within the Marauder paradigm. </div> </div> </div>There's no such thing. Being a Marauder is not a matter of paradigm. It's a metaphysical state brought on by the consequences of the reality warping powers mages possess going awry. Marauders can come from any paradigm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Religion is supposed to be about humility... </div> </div> </div>Nope. Stop.<br /> <br /> It's fine if you want to have a discussion about how to define religion vs. similar concepts, but do not presume to attribute a value or belief to all religions. Religion is a diverse phenomenon, with diverse beliefs and values.<br /> <br /> If we're talking about the Chorus, we're technically talking about The One anyway, and characters are (ideally) free to approach The One without the dogma of other Chorister's personal approaches. How a Christian Chorister chooses to make their supplications is not a requirement on how a Deist Chorister that rejects any Sleeper organized religion's practices supplicates the One.<br /> <br /> Besides the fact that you're skipping both Christian Elitist philosophies (various Christian sects that believe as the chosen elite it is impossible for them to sin because they were selected to represent righteous actions), and transactional religious practices (where adherents believe their deity/deities are bound into contracts with believers and must uphold their end of things if supplicated properly), you're running to a semantic nitpick to dodge the point being made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T22:56:48-08:00","id":1033176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1032879#post1032879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If my paradigm as a Celestial Chorister is &quot;God makes His miracles work through me,&quot; then it's really hard to justify why any particular Sphere effect is out of bounds. Unless you're trying to argue that the Chorister would see that God is somehow limited in His actions, and therefore can't generate a cloak of invisibility around the Chorister using Forces 3, or give them the ability to fly like an Angel with Forces 3, or let them call down fire from Heaven with Forces 3...<br /> <br /> ...or become an invisible, flying predator drone while calling down fire from the heavens using multiple Forces 3 effects...</div> </div> </div> </div>I can think of at least one explanation for why said Chorister's magick would be limited, even if God's isn't: &quot;Of course God CAN do anything. But there may be things He WON'T do, nor allow to be done just because I ask for it.&quot; Just because God exists and is all powerful doesn't mean He doesn't also have standards and plans of His own.<br /> <br /> Effectively, it constrains the Mage not by what they think is possible, but what is acceptable. Certain Effects they could construe as morally repugnant, such as animating corpses (not to be confused with True Resurrection) or driving someone to insanity or making them feel physically or mentally violated, are off limits. They cannot ask certain things of God, because they are awful things that no man should do unto another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T02:02:58-08:00","id":1033240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1033176#post1033176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because God exists and is all powerful doesn't mean He doesn't also have standards and plans of His own.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes far more sense as how such a mage rationalizes a failed spell (or even Paradox) than not actually being able to try the effect at all.<br /> <br /> As well, a given mage finding a given application of magic morally repugnant doesn't mean they don't believe it is possible. If your mage believes that necromancy is too morally corrupt to deal in, their paradigm also inherently accepts that it is possible to do. There's no point in believing your chosen deity came down and said, &quot;Do not do X, it is forbidden!&quot; if X was impossible to do. If you believe it is forbidden, you also believe it possible (even if there are good reasons it is forbidden and the results cannot conform to your expectations for them).<br /> <br /> There is a huge difference between being unwilling to do something, and being unable to do something. Even in mage paradigm doesn't stretch so far as to enforce your morality on your magic for you (if it did, the Euthanatos wouldn't have so much trouble with Jhor for doing what they believe is a moral good).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T02:12:58-08:00","id":1033243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1033240#post1033240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That makes far more sense as how such a mage rationalizes a failed spell (or even Paradox) than not actually being able to try the effect at all.<br /> <br /> As well, a given mage finding a given application of magic morally repugnant doesn't mean they don't believe it is possible. If your mage believes that necromancy is too morally corrupt to deal in, their paradigm also inherently accepts that it is possible to do. There's no point in believing your chosen deity came down and said, &quot;Do not do X, it is forbidden!&quot; if X was impossible to do. If you believe it is forbidden, you also believe it possible (even if there are good reasons it is forbidden and the results cannot conform to your expectations for them).<br /> <br /> There is a huge difference between being unwilling to do something, and being unable to do something. Even in mage paradigm doesn't stretch so far as to enforce your morality on your magic for you (if it did, the Euthanatos wouldn't have so much trouble with Jhor for doing what they believe is a moral good).</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is that, if the Mage believes their magic comes directly from God, and something is morally wrong, that <i>God will refuse to answer the prayer</i>. It doesn't matter if it's technically possible for God to do it, the limit of the <i>Mage's</i> magick is what they believe God will do for them if they ask.<br /> <br /> It ceases to be a question of &quot;Is this possible?&quot;, and becomes &quot;Can the <i>Mage</i> do it, given the methods they have?&quot; And if the Mage gets his power from God's grace, that power is limited to what he thinks God will allow. If the Mage doesn't think God would answer a prayer to make corpses dance like puppets on a string, it's not going to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T02:21:12-08:00","id":1033244,"title":"","content":"The only way it is &quot;sure&quot; to not happen is because the mage in question isn't going to try it; not because paradigm is limiting them from being able to do it.<br /> <br /> Besides, the Old Testament is full of examples of calling for somewhat silly minor miracles just to demonstrate divine power. There is literally a, &quot;who's deity is better at turning staves into snakes&quot; contest in there just for Moses to prove who's got the best one. You don't have to stretch much or look hard to know that those wielding divine grace in holy texts have been granted some pretty big leeway in what miracles they've been granted the power to perform.<br /> <br /> If a mage has a reason to try and have the &quot;miracle of the dancing skeletons&quot; be a thing, then they can pray and see if it happens or not (aka if they fail the spell or not). They're not getting hard locked out by their paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T03:03:13-08:00","id":1033249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1033244#post1033244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only way it is &quot;sure&quot; to not happen is because the mage in question isn't going to try it; not because paradigm is limiting them from being able to do it.<br /> <br /> Besides, the Old Testament is full of examples of calling for somewhat silly minor miracles just to demonstrate divine power. There is literally a, &quot;who's deity is better at turning staves into snakes&quot; contest in there just for Moses to prove who's got the best one. You don't have to stretch much or look hard to know that those wielding divine grace in holy texts have been granted some pretty big leeway in what miracles they've been granted the power to perform.<br /> <br /> If a mage has a reason to try and have the &quot;miracle of the dancing skeletons&quot; be a thing, then they can pray and see if it happens or not (aka if they fail the spell or not). They're not getting hard locked out by their paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a difference between performing a miracle to prove God can do something, and performing what, by the ethics of the religion in question, would be a profane and unholy feat. Despite the, shall we say, permissive attitudes about the morality of necromancy we have here on the Mage forum, it's an art that is pretty soundly denounced by most of Western culture. I know for a fact that the Bible forbids contacting the dead, so making them dance is probably out of the question. And I can't imagine any other flavor of worship of The One being much more okay with it.<br /> <br /> That's just animating dead bodies. What about <i>summoning demons</i>? Pardon the pun, but there's no way in hell God would do that for the Chorister. Infernal beings are the enemies of heaven, and should not be consorted with under any circumstance. Even if you try to claim it's to get a spirit being to do something for the Mage, why isn't the character summoning an angel? Doing anything with a devil other than forcing from a possessed person and casting it back into the pit is unacceptable by all but the most troubling interpretations of theology, unless you happen to be a member of the Wu Lung (which are a whole other kettle of fish, with their own restrictions mandated by the Divine Bureaucracy).<br /> <br /> And the Chorister would know that. At least they would if they had a defensible interpretation of theology. If they believed God to be good, they naturally wouldn't expect God to answer a prayer for an unholy act. Not because God couldn't foster the presence of True Evil in the world, but because He's not in the business of shooting Himself in the foot. Not when His plans revolve around defeating Evil. Hell is not divided against itself. Why would Heaven be?<br /> <br /> <br /> But let's get to the meat of the matter. This idea that the Mage would see that anything is possible, because they'll try anything once, just to see if it works. Let's set aside the fact that the Chorister is making the mistake of disobeying the order not to test the Lord your God. Let's instead focus on the fact that it puts the cart before the horse. The entire reason Mage Paradigms have restrictions is because they adhere to an internal logic about what a Mage can and cannot do. Not what might be possible for The One, but what the <i>Mage</i> is capable of. That, according to their world view, X can be done if they do Y, and Z cannot be done. It's inherent to the Focus system.<br /> <br /> A Void Engineer cannot awaken the spirit of an object, because the Void Engineer does not believe in an animistic reality. Nor can that VE even try to do so, because his Paradigm presupposes it to be impossible. If some Traditionalist told him &quot;have you ever tried talking to your gun?&quot;, the VE would naturally think the supersititionist is an idiot. Trying to awaken the spirit of an item won't work unless he already believes it is possible. It's a Catch 22.<br /> <br /> As it is with the Chorister. The morality of certain acts - and therefore whether God would bother empowering a Mage to do them - is baked into the Paradigm from the start. Either he believes The One has standards He won't go against, if which case that assumption will be proven correct when the experiment fails, or he believes The One has no real moral standards and just lets His agents do whatever immoral thing they want - in His name - in which case that assumption will be proven correct when the experiment succeeds. It's Confirmation Bias that feeds itself, and is dependent on the character already believing whatever they expect to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T04:32:36-08:00","id":1033263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1033249#post1033249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a difference between performing a miracle to prove God can do something, and performing what, by the ethics of the religion in question, would be a profane and unholy feat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither of which has any bearing one whether or not the paradigm says it is possible to do, and thus is possible for the mage to do if even it would be bad by their moral standards to do so. I don't see what the issue here is... mages are not paragons of virtue. They're supposed to be flawed and subject to the temptations of using their powers in ways that go against their ideals. If you force their morality as a hard limitation into their paradigm, mages then literally can't do bad things (by their standards at least) with magic; which clearly goes against the entire premise and spirit of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Despite the, shall we say, permissive attitudes about the morality of necromancy we have here on the Mage forum, it's an art that is pretty soundly denounced by most of Western culture. I know for a fact that the Bible forbids contacting the dead, so making them dance is probably out of the question. </div> </div> </div>The Bible forbids it... and then tells a story of a guy that does it anyway (and in fact had just reaffirmed said prohibition to the people). The Bible both says not to do it, and says it is completely possible to do. If the Bible is the guide to your mage's paradigm, their paradigm accepts necromancy as something you can do with magic. Their moral stance on the subject is a separate matter, and just like Saul they might spout off about how it's forbidden, and then find themselves desperate to talk to someone that's already dead and make the choice to do so.<br /> <br /> Again, there is nothing in the books that supports intertwining moral objections with paradigm. What you believe is good is not the same as what you believe is possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What about <i>summoning demons</i>? Pardon the pun, but there's no way in hell God would do that for the Chorister. </div> </div> </div>Worked out pretty well for Solomon. The ability to command demons (including summoning them) is a fairly classic ability for those blessed with divine grace so that they can then trap and deal with said demons to neutralize them. Besides the fact that not every religion (or iteration of Christianity for that matter) holds the views you're portraying regarding demons and what's acceptable in how to deal with them, demonology is a lot standing practice. Most religions where this is an issue do not hold that you can just say a few prayers to defeat any and all demons. Some demons are too powerful and must be bound in deals and similar tricks to keep the world safe from them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Infernal beings are the enemies of heaven, and should not be consorted with under any circumstance. </div> </div> </div>How do you perform an exorcism if you can't talk to demons and command them back to hell?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Doing anything with a devil other than forcing from a possessed person and casting it back into the pit is unacceptable by all but the most troubling interpretations of theology... </div> </div> </div>Not... really? I mean what on Earth is this assertion based on?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they believed God to be good, they naturally wouldn't expect God to answer a prayer for an unholy act. </div> </div> </div>Right, which only applies if the mage is purposefully trying to do something &quot;unholy&quot; and thus wouldn't do it. If they've gone &quot;evil&quot; they'd absolutely try to deceive miracles out of the divine. If they're just desperate they will try to justify their actions as righteous bending of the rules. In either case though, their paradigm still lets them try to pull it off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not because God couldn't foster the presence of True Evil in the world, but because He's not in the business of shooting Himself in the foot. </div> </div> </div>There's plenty of functional theology that does assume the divine is &quot;shooting themselves in the foot,&quot; mostly in order to spurn humanity to take up the place meant for them by their own will instead of divine mandate. I am, have you read Judges? It's just one long spiral of shooting yourself in the foot on a metaphysical level.<br /> <br /> And of course, most Choristers would not believe in a knowable One, so all these assumptions about what the One wants, intends, etc., would be perceived as speculation at best.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The entire reason Mage Paradigms have restrictions is because they adhere to an internal logic about what a Mage can and cannot do. </div> </div> </div>Except this isn't true. The purpose of paradigm is to make the mage adhere to an internal logic about how that mage does magic. Any restrictions or limitations are secondary effects from the core concept of how. The &quot;Creating Other Paradigms&quot; section of M20 does not bring up once the idea of designing what a mage can and cannot do when creating a new paradigm. It talks about the kinds of beliefs necessary to bolster an effective paradigm that mage can leverage to use magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Void Engineer cannot awaken the spirit of an object, because the Void Engineer does not believe in an animistic reality. </div> </div> </div>Window dressing with a bit of the VE using Dimension Science instead of the Spirit Sphere.<br /> <br /> A VE can't awaken the spirit of an object, sure. They can, however, use the Anthropic Principle Field to find a subdimension populated by EDEs that correspond to platonic ideals of physical objects and then reconfigure their tool to harness that thought form for improved function.<br /> <br /> The VE can't lay their hands on someone to heal them either, they use hypertech medkits.<br /> <br /> The VE will find &quot;talking to his gun,&quot; or, &quot;laying of hands,&quot; equally silly, but that doesn't mean the VE doesn't have their own ways to achieve the same effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T06:19:39-08:00","id":1033303,"title":"","content":"So, I take that some people see Mage as a game about playing nascent gods (True Magick allows my character to do anything, regardless of Paradigm, and STs are mean and wrong if they try to enforce rules of Paradigm or Paradox that interfere with my character's quest for ultimate power) instead of a game that explores that essential questions of what it means to be human (power corrupts, absolute power corrupts absolutely, so Paradigm and Paradox exists to prevent me from being corrupted absolutely by preventing me from gaining absolute power). In my games, I use Paradigm and Paradox to make True Magick special. In effect, I try to preserve the wonder of my players in True Magick by not allowing them to get bored by using True Magick for every trivial task.<br /> <br /> While a member of the Order of Hermes could create a portal from NY to Tokyo, there are airplanes and, except for emergencies, why would he defile the purity of his Great Art to avoid minor inconveniences? While a member of the Celestial Choir could depend on God to protect them, God helps those who help themselves, so it is sacrilegious to expect God to show her special favor when she could just get a concealed carry permit for a gun. True Magick is supposed to be magnificent, it is not supposed to be wasted of mundane concerns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T06:35:07-08:00","id":1033315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1033249#post1033249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a difference between performing a miracle to prove God can do something, and performing what, by the ethics of the religion in question, would be a profane and unholy feat.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet all of the examples you choose have Biblical justification for them. A generic Christian Chorister can point to their own holy book if the ST of the particular game was to try to say, &quot;In your paradigm it doesn't make sense for your character to ask for that.&quot; I'll go through them one by one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1033249#post1033249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Necromancy...</div> </div> </div> </div>Acts 20: Seated in a window was a young man named Eutychus, who was sinking into a deep sleep as Paul talked on and on. When he was sound asleep, he fell to the ground from the third story and was picked up dead. Paul went down, threw himself on the young man and put his arms around him. \u201cDon\u2019t be alarmed,\u201d he said. \u201cHe\u2019s alive!\u201d Then he went upstairs again and broke bread and ate. After talking until daylight, he left. The people took the young man home alive and were greatly comforted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or driving someone to insanity or making them feel physically or mentally violated </div> </div> </div>Deuteronomy: The Lord will smite you with madness, blindness and with bewilderment of heart.<br /> <br /> 1 Samuel: Now it came about on the next day that an evil spirit from God came mightily upon Saul, and he raved in the midst of the house<br /> <br /> Daniel: While the word was in the king\u2019s mouth, a voice came from heaven, saying, \u2018King Nebuchadnezzar, to you it is declared: sovereignty has been removed from you, and you will be driven away from mankind, and your dwelling place will be with the beasts of the field. You will be given grass to eat like cattle, and seven periods of time will pass over you until you recognize that the Most High is ruler over the realm of mankind and bestows it on whomever He wishes....But at the end of that period, I, Nebuchadnezzar, raised my eyes toward heaven and <u><i><b>my reason returned to me</b></i></u>, and I blessed the Most High and praised and honored Him who lives forever; For His dominion is an everlasting dominion, And His kingdom endures from generation to generation.<br /> <br /> The Old Testament is full of examples of God sending evil spirits to torment people who defy Him or disobey him. Hell, God will even torment innocent, righteous people for the purposes of winning a bet (Book of Job.) It's hard to say that a Chorister using Mind to drive people into madness can't be justified with the religion, let alone the paradigm of &quot;praying for miracles.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What about <i>summoning demons</i>? Pardon the pun, but there's no way in hell God would do that for the Chorister. </div> </div> </div>Do you know what this is?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Seal_of_Solomon_(Simple_Version).svg/220px-Seal_of_Solomon_(Simple_Version).svg.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> It's the symbol on a signet ring that was worn and used by the greatest demonic summoner and binder of all time. That guy's name, spoiler, was Solomon. Old Testament Guy. You might have heard of him. <br /> <br /> The Book of Mark said that Jesus &quot;And he called the twelve and began to send them out two by two, and gave them authority over the unclean spirits.&quot; From the book of Matthew, it is said of the church founded on Peter &quot;I will give you the keys of the kingdom of heaven; and whatever you shall bind on earth shall be bound in heaven, and whatever you shall loose on earth shall be loosed in heaven.&quot;<br /> <br /> So yeah. I'm seeing that if a Chorister wanted to summon, bind, or loose demons, he has ample justification for doing so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Void Engineer cannot awaken the spirit of an object, because the Void Engineer does not believe in an animistic reality. Nor can that VE even try to do so, because his Paradigm presupposes it to be impossible. If some Traditionalist told him &quot;have you ever tried talking to your gun?&quot;, the VE would naturally think the supersititionist is an idiot. Trying to awaken the spirit of an item won't work unless he already believes it is possible. It's a Catch 22. </div> </div> </div>And yet, the Guide to the Traditions I quoted earlier is very specific; if you have either a liberal paradigm you can pick up rotes and effects of other Traditions. The Hermetic can learn breathing exercises from the Akashic monk to sharpen his memory, a Verbena could learn a fire-lighting song from a Dreamspeaker, and a Void Engineer could learn the 'find a good parking spot in the garage search pattern' from a New World Order field agent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As it is with the Chorister. The morality of certain acts - and therefore whether God would bother empowering a Mage to do them - is baked into the Paradigm from the start. Either he believes The One has standards He won't go against, if which case that assumption will be proven correct when the experiment fails, or he believes The One has no real moral standards and just lets His agents do whatever immoral thing they want - in His name - in which case that assumption will be proven correct when the experiment succeeds. It's Confirmation Bias that feeds itself, and is dependent on the character already believing whatever they expect to happen. </div> </div> </div>...and? I mean, this is kind of a non sequitur. The original argument as I understand it is whether or not paradigm should be used by STs to restrict the kinds of effects a Mage should be able to generate using his Spheres. We've wandered into a discussion about a valid paradigm, a Chorister who prays for miracles. HA and I have pretty much argued that just about any effect the Chorister wants is possible under that paradigm. Your reply is that it's confirmation bias....so what? How is that any different from the confirmation bias that confronts a Hermetic any time he says a spell from his master's spell book that throws magic missiles at his enemy. &quot;It worked so therefore my paradigm is correct.&quot; Or the Technocratic doctor who treats his patients with hyper-antibiotics. &quot;See, his reaction to this drug proves that his illness was caused by microbes.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T06:36:43-08:00","id":1033316,"title":"","content":"Religions, and religious views, are very varied, and what's ethical for one isn't for other. Having said that:<br /> <br /> If you believe that God it's omniscient, and has moral, and that all power comes from him, then of course you won't be able to pray to him for atrocities (read: thigs he wouldn't do acording to your beliefs). It would be as silly as talking to his gun to awaken it's spirit for a VE.<br /> However, such belief it's as shallow as believing that God can do anything and it's your bitch. The very fact that atrocities occur in the world defies it.<br /> Then, let's say you add Satan to justify that. Well, now you know who have you to pray to get atricities done.<br /> <br /> However this adds a point where I think that Bluecho argument it's correct. A Christian may believe that there are ways to make the dead dance, or summon demons, but probably Praying isn't one of them. Thus Paradigms aren't limmited by moral, however, Practices and Instruments may be fueled by moral. You don't use holy prayer to summon demons to do your bidding , you use Goetia instead (In some versions of Christianism you may be able to do it with prayer, but not in all of them).<br /> This can act like a limitation, because Practices and Instruments are thing you need to learn how to use. The fact that this isn't always going to be the case doesn't mean that it can't be. If you need a medic kit to heal because you don't believe in imposing hands, then you may need to learn medicine to use it. This it's a limitation, you think it's possible, but you can't do it. The Christian may need to learn Goetia to summon his demon<br /> <br /> EDIT: BTW, saying that your paradigm it's &quot;God it's omnipotent and makes His milacres trough me when I pray&quot; it's no less silly than saying my paradigm it's that &quot;I'm omnipotent, and work in misterious ways granting power to myself when I brush my hear&quot;. This is why Paradigms are described in more than one line. Why God makes it's will trough you?, Why when you are praying?, why do you need to do anything at all so god manifests it's magick?. Paradigm needs some flesh, at the very least it has to justify the Focus","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-17-2017, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T06:51:50-08:00","id":1033326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1033303#post1033303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While a member of the Order of Hermes could create a portal from NY to Tokyo, there are airplanes and, except for emergencies, why would he defile the purity of his Great Art to avoid minor inconveniences? While a member of the Celestial Choir could depend on God to protect them, God helps those who help themselves, so it is sacrilegious to expect God to show her special favor when she could just get a concealed carry permit for a gun. True Magick is supposed to be magnificent, it is not supposed to be wasted of mundane concerns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Harry Dresden has a magic spell he created to light the candles in his apartment. It's called 'Flickum Bicus.' (For those that never got the reference, BIC is the brand name of very common plastic lighters). Characters in Harry Potter travel by several different methods of magical teleportation for such mundane reasons as back to school shopping, attending sporting events, and going downstairs to check on breakfast. Quicksilver in the X-Men movies uses his super-speed to blitz through Ms. Pacman. In D&amp;D, there's a 0-th level cantrip that cleans your clothes. In Discworld there's an enchanted piece of luggage that follows its owner around to spare him the trouble of actually picking up a heavy box. In The Blade Itself, the wizard Bayaz makes a bunch of thugs and assassins explode in the same room that his allies with swords are hanging about. In the Name of the Wind, Ambrose uses magic to break the lute string of another character trying to give a performance in front of a crowd to sabotage his act. In the Fellowship of the Rings, Gandalf uses his magic to create animate fireworks displays (especially relevant, as Gandalf was an angel in Tolkien's cosmology). In Mistborn, Kelsier uses his allomancy to travel great distances at speed. In the Wheel of Time, there's discussion that the Seanchan use Earth channelers to find valuable mineral deposits and excavate the ground to facilitate building and construction.<br /> <br /> Popular fiction, from which many players draw their inspiration for their Mage characters, abounds...literally abounds, with examples of magic-using folk using magic to accomplish mundane feats. Frankly, your statement that magic should be special and not used on mundane concerns is looking more and more like your own hangup here. And I'm also going to point out that the things you mentioned that should be preferable for a Traditions Mage, flying an airplane or using a gun instead of using Correspondence or Forces effects, are borrowing from the paradigm of the Technocracy. Airplanes only fly and guns only work as weapons because the Technocracy has convinced the world that Bernoulli's Principle can be used for flight or that contained chemical explosions can propel a projectile. Why are you insisting that the Traditions eschew their own paradigms and bow before the scientific paradigm of the Technocracy? Paradigm is everything, right? Why should the Hermetic be forced to adopt Technocratic Correspondance and Forces applications?<br /> <br /> You say that True MagicK is supposed to be magnificent. And also that Mage is a game about being human. I say to you that finding trivial, silly, irreverent, and selfish applications for anything is very much in keeping with human nature. Case in point, we have at our literal fingertips the most sophisticated means of information storage and retrieval and communication than anyone has ever enjoyed in any time period in history. It's called the Internet.<br /> <br /> And the Internet is for porn. Talk about triviliazing True MagicK.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":1515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","user":"BenjCano","date":". 01-17-2017, 05:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T14:20:28-08:00","id":1033638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1033303#post1033303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I take that some people see Mage as a game about playing nascent gods (True Magick allows my character to do anything, regardless of Paradigm, and STs are mean and wrong if they try to enforce rules of Paradigm or Paradox that interfere with my character's quest for ultimate power) instead of a game that explores that essential questions of what it means to be human (power corrupts, absolute power corrupts absolutely, so Paradigm and Paradox exists to prevent me from being corrupted absolutely by preventing me from gaining absolute power).</div> </div> </div> </div>Strawmen don't do any of us any good. Nobody said you can ignore paradigm, just that paradigm isn't the limitation people are making it out to be. Nobody said anything at all about skipping out on the Paradox rules.<br /> <br /> Nobody is saying that Mage is inherently a game about nascent &quot;gods&quot; (though it certainly has to include that since apotheosis should be something mages can peruse!).<br /> <br /> Mage is a game about the consequences of god-like power in the hands of human beings. If you get so heavy-handed with the &quot;limitations of Paradigm,&quot; that you deny the players the chance to explore just how powerful they are, you deny the story to get around to the horrific consequences of people that have no better grasp of morals and ethics than any other human getting access to all that power. I never get to explore my mage's arrogance if any time they think that they can bend the rules and push things the &quot;wrong&quot; way, the ST steps in and says, &quot;No no no, that's not in paradigm enough you can't even try that!&quot;<br /> <br /> How about this, cite us a passage where the game tells us that the ST should use the fact that a mage's magic should follow their paradigm to stop the player from trying something. That limitation is there, but the books don't tell us to smack players with it, they tell us to craft magic with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In my games, I use Paradigm and Paradox to make True Magick special. </div> </div> </div>Sounds dreadfully unfun to me. When I'm playing Mage, I want to, you know, play the game. I want to define my character and play my character, not the ST's idea of what my character should be. I don't see where the books tell us the ST's job is to ensure the 'wonder' of magic by being super-heavy handed with game concepts to control the play experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While a member of the Order of Hermes could create a portal from NY to Tokyo, there are airplanes and, except for emergencies, why would he defile the purity of his Great Art to avoid minor inconveniences? </div> </div> </div>Why would you defile the great technological feat of flight by using it for anything but the most monumental efforts? You should just walk everywhere unless it's a vital situation to respect technology. Oh... wait... that's not how power works. Easy to access power gets used.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> True Magick is supposed to be magnificent, it is not supposed to be wasted of mundane concerns. </div> </div> </div>And mages are humans. We're very prone to apply the magnificent to the mundane.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1033316#post1033316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you believe that God it's omniscient, and has moral, and that all power comes from him, then of course you won't be able to pray to him for atrocities (read: thigs he wouldn't do acording to your beliefs).</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is of course, that you have to consider it an atrocity.<br /> <br /> It's not your paradigm stopping you. It's you stopping you. A mage that would be willing to bomb a city flat and kill millions isn't going to balk at supplicating a deity to do it magically instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The very fact that atrocities occur in the world defies it. </div> </div> </div>Not really. If we're going Biblical... there's plenty of things that people on the receiving end would call an atrocity that got called miracles. I'm pretty sure the Biblical Egyptians weren't like, &quot;Dude, that Israelite supreme deity sure is great for killing all our first born children. Lets give them all our material wealth because that was just such a morally great thing and we're not giving up our silver because we're afraid to be slaughtered next just because Pharaoh's going to back out on his deal.&quot;<br /> <br /> You don't need Satan to explain why bad things happen. There's plenty of simple shallow ways to address it that still allow your appeals to all go to the same place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Christian may believe that there are ways to make the dead dance, or summon demons, but probably Praying isn't one of them. </div> </div> </div>Quibbling over instruments is, however, already acknowledging the larger point that paradigm doesn't cause a significant limitation here. It's not a matter of can/cannot but of how. Picking the best tools of your trade for the task at hand isn't the same issue as if you can't perform the task at hand even if you're not using the best tools. As well, remember that a mage might see multiple different instruments as defined in the system as all forms of prayer. &quot;Silent prayer&quot; is meditation, for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This can act like a limitation, because Practices and Instruments are thing you need to learn how to use. </div> </div> </div>Yes. This is much more the point (and explicitly in the books something that's harsher on technomages anyway). How you do things is what matters, and thus mages tend to need to be good<br /> at how they do things. However this is also one of the advantages of the formal paradigms common among groups like the Hermetics or the Chorus. Their strength is in standardizing such things and making them logical and simple to access instead of relying on self-discovering or experimentation (at least at first). Their libraries have appropriate specific instruments for everything. &quot;There's a prayer for that&quot; already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> BTW, saying that your paradigm it's &quot;God it's omnipotent and makes His milacres trough me when I pray&quot; it's no less silly than saying my paradigm it's that &quot;I'm omnipotent, and work in misterious ways granting power to myself when I brush my hear&quot;. </div> </div> </div>True for playing the game, but a bit nitpicky for trying to discuss it. Having to a fully flushed out Focus for every example we make is just tedious and exhausting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T07:44:16-08:00","id":1034009,"title":"","content":"Yes, well, I think that the point that I was trying to convey was understood. If a certain morality it's part of the paradigm, this has to be addressed in the way effect are shaped, albeit it's the 'how' more than the 'if' what limmits effects. After all, a strong paradigm should be able to explain, if not everything, almost everything that happens.<br /> <br /> I think your point it's generaly true because a Paradigm it's a cosmovision, and thus it's <i>meant</i> to be very inclusive.<br /> This doesn't mean that it's impossible for your paradigm to limmit what you can do, even when that limitation it's likely to be contingent, and probably it will manifest by limiting how a thing it's supposed to be done (If you have no how, then you can't <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ). Only in that limmited way I think that a Paradigm does/should limmit what a mage can do.<br /> I also think that streeeeeeeeeching the limmits of your paradigm, the flavor of your magick, to be able to do an effect that you need in the moment it's bad roleplaying, as it's often very noticeable <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . But if isn't blatant, then go for it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem is of course, that you have to consider it an atrocity.<br /> <br /> It's not your paradigm stopping you. It's you stopping you. A mage that would be willing to bomb a city flat and kill millions isn't going to balk at supplicating a deity to do it magically instead.<br /> <br /> If we're going Biblical... there's plenty of things that people on the receiving end would call an atrocity that got called miracles. </div> </div> </div>He would balk if he believes it isn't going to work because (this) god doesn't answer these kinds of prayer <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I wasn't going biblical, I was making a mockery of religion to explain how such mockeries are paradigmatically weak, thus enabling the user to &quot;do almost everything&quot;, or &quot;do very little&quot;, dependingon how they're worded.<br /> <br /> I'm a bit tired of everyone using &quot;I believe in god's omnipotency&quot; to justify that their mages can do everything. Why?, because they put god there just because they know that if they used a paradigm that says &quot;I believe i'm omnipotent and can do everything&quot;, the answer would be that such Paradigm it's unadmisible, and they know that if god is there instead of just personal omnipotence, they will believe that they're refering to a perfectly reasonable Chorister.<br /> But in truth they're inventing a universal believer that can use whatever belief fit's the moment. Disregarding that every VALID paradigm has a flavor that limmits what you would do, that it's, the ways to do it (which may as well be closed for you). That isn't different from saying that your paradigm it's to be omnipotent, it's just a sophism to make believable that your mage can do everything disregarding flavor, style, instruments, and every step that you should accomplish to do something.<br /> In the end, this doesn't prove that Paradigm shouldn't limmit what you can do, it only proves that some Paradigms limmit you less than others, to the point that they may be overpowered, if ain't checked somehow.<br /> <br /> In other words, you're building a believable mock paradigm that can do whatever you want, but you aren't proving that the opposite (a Paradigm that limmits what you can do) doesn't exist, or isn't more believable/interesting than the one that let's you do anything. How does defending any of this help YOUR point?.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-18-2017, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T08:26:58-08:00","id":1034026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1034009#post1034009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end, this doesn't prove that Paradigm shouldn't limmit what you can do, it only proves that some Paradigms limmit you less than others, to the point that they may be overpowered, if ain't checked somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is kind of a 'duh.' If your paradigm is &quot;I found a magic ring on a dying alien that lets me wield hard light projections', then you lose your ability to use magic if that ring is taken from you. If your paradigm is &quot;I can heal any disease by brewing a concoction of all natural herbs,&quot; then you can't use your magic if you don't have access to the herbs you think you need. If your paradigm is, &quot;by speaking aloud the secret True Names of elemental forces, I can bind and command those forces,&quot; then you can't use your magic if you're gagged.<br /> <br /> If your paradigm is &quot;I can read and control minds because I'm Professor Xavier,&quot; then you don't have those built-in limitations I just mentioned. Why should you be OK with the 'gifted genetic psychic' paradigm that allows pretty much unlimited use of effects in the Mind Sphere, but balk at the Chorister going &quot;my paradigm is to ask for miracles that God opts to grant or deny as He sees fit&quot; and trying to use any Forces effect he wants?<br /> <br /> I really don't think that it's up to the ST to arbitrarily state &quot;You need to write a graduate thesis on the theological implications of your cosmology&quot; before letting a player play Mage. What, precisely, is the downside to a player playing a powerful character? You can't just throw words like &quot;It might be overpowered and therefore we have to limit what players can do&quot; if you don't establish what exactly overpowered means and why it's a bad thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":1515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","user":"BenjCano","date":". 01-18-2017, 11:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T08:45:13-08:00","id":1034036,"title":"","content":"But there is a difference between asking God and telling God. Asking God is asking the ST to rule on the effect and then rolling after ST approval. Telling God is telling the ST what the effect is and then acting outraged if the ST denies the effect as inappropriate for your Paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T08:52:30-08:00","id":1034042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1034036#post1034036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Telling God is telling the ST what the effect is and then acting outraged if the ST denies the effect as inappropriate for your Paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Imagine that. The player wants to determine the specifics of his character's religious belief. How is asking about whether a Chorister's paradigm would allow a particular effect be any different from the conversation, &quot;Does my bald mutant psychic believe he can erase or modify memories using his mutant psychic powers?&quot;<br /> <br /> My experience with &quot;can I use X Sphere to do Y effect,&quot; has always been to have the ST turn around and say to me &quot;Does your character think he can?&quot; Or &quot;How does he believe that using his foci the way he's doing will result in the effect you want?&quot;<br /> <br /> I've NEVER had a ST tell me that the effect I wanted with the foci I was using was inappropriate because my character wouldn't believe that was possible. If my noir-ish detective wants to use Correspondance/Entropy by throwing darts at a map of the city to locate the missing child he's been hired to retrieve, I'd be rightly peeved if the ST said, &quot;No your character wouldn't use his magic that way because he'd never think that'd work or be something that random chance and subconscious deductions would lead him to do.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'd be similarly peeved if I was playing a Chorister and prayed for an Effect and got told, &quot;No, sorry. Your character's religion doesn't allow that.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":1515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","user":"BenjCano","date":". 01-18-2017, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T08:52:44-08:00","id":1034043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1034036#post1034036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there is a difference between asking God and telling God. Asking God is asking the ST to rule on the effect and then rolling after ST approval. Telling God is telling the ST what the effect is and then acting outraged if the ST denies the effect as inappropriate for your Paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also a difference between the Character not knowing how the spell is going to play out and the Player not knowing how the spell is going to work out. It is entirely possible to define the effect even if your character doesn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T10:19:53-08:00","id":1034106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1034009#post1034009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think that streeeeeeeeeching the limmits of your paradigm, the flavor of your magick, to be able to do an effect that you need in the moment it's bad roleplaying, as it's often very noticeable</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why are there rules in the books for doing exactly that? The fact that you can (at great penalty) overcome your restrictions on &quot;how&quot; through will illustrates that the game completely encourages role-playing mages as the kind of people that would consider doing it when desperate. If the book says, &quot;if you're denied your 'how' you can still try magic,&quot; it's pretty hard to justify the ST saying, &quot;no that's bad role-playing.&quot; The ST has mechanical penalties to lay down for characters knowingly acting at the edges of what their paradigm calls for.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He would balk if he believes it isn't going to work because (this) god doesn't answer these kinds of prayer. </div> </div> </div>But, again, paradigms that have staying power do so because they tend to be inclusive. As fun as a thought exercise that might be, mages will prefer the interpretations of their beliefs that give them the greatest leeway in creating magical effects; M20 directly says this is the case no less.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm a bit tired of everyone using &quot;I believe in god's omnipotency&quot; to justify that their mages can do everything. </div> </div> </div>Again, remember this is an Internet conversation, a lot of the &quot;go to&quot; examples are used because they're simple to say and easy to understand; not because they're as deep as an actual play paradigm should be. It's also tiring when people try to continually nitpick incomplete examples for being incomplete whether or not the example in question illustrates the point trying to be made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the end, this doesn't prove that Paradigm shouldn't limmit what you can do, it only proves that some Paradigms limmit you less than others, to the point that they may be overpowered, if ain't checked somehow. </div> </div> </div>Again, M20 actually addresses a lot of this in discussing paradigms (and specifically what sort of beliefs and structures make for successful paradigms). What you're calling &quot;overpowered&quot; it basically calls the default: most mages go for the most permissible paradigms in the end.<br /> <br /> Paradigms aren't mean to be a &quot;check&quot; on character power, they're meant to be a framing device for your character's magic. The &quot;checks&quot; in the system are numerous and largely come in the form of consequences for your character's choices (which is, again, a major theme of the game) rather than limitations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How does defending any of this help YOUR point?. </div> </div> </div>Please see above point about the tedium of people treating shallow examples as bad for being shallow rather than failing to make the point trying to be made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1034036#post1034036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there is a difference between asking God and telling God.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in the mechanics of the game there isn't. A Chorister praying as a request, and a Hermetic using mystic rules to command, both use the same mechanics to adjudicate the results. The Chorister is not putting themselves in a special position of ST fiat on how their magic works.<br /> <br /> Also, I find it rather telling that you're basically claiming that the role of the ST in this circumstance is to be a supreme deity at the table.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T10:45:49-08:00","id":1034113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1034036#post1034036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there is a difference between asking God and telling God. Asking God is asking the ST to rule on the effect and then rolling after ST approval. Telling God is telling the ST what the effect is and then acting outraged if the ST denies the effect as inappropriate for your Paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>But in the game there is no God. It's the mage in question doing magic, not God. If Timmy the Chorister decides to ask God to conjure him a cup of coffee, then that means Timmy already internally accepts the idea that God might grant this request. Or he wouldn't ask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T11:27:11-08:00","id":1034131,"title":"","content":"Or maybe Timmy it's acting out of character, because his player it's metagaming.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your paradigm is &quot;I can read and control minds because I'm Professor Xavier,&quot; then you don't have those built-in limitations I just mentioned. Why should you be OK with the 'gifted genetic psychic' paradigm that allows pretty much unlimited use of effects in the Mind Sphere, but balk at the Chorister going &quot;my paradigm is to ask for miracles that God opts to grant or deny as He sees fit&quot; and trying to use any Forces effect he wants?<br /> ...<br /> How is asking about whether a Chorister's paradigm would allow a particular effect be any different from the conversation, &quot;Does my bald mutant psychic believe he can erase or modify memories using his mutant psychic powers?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Does your psychic believes he can summon angels?. If not, then he can't. Oh, but you're <i>very clever</i>, so you will summon <i>&quot;aliens&quot;</i>, not &quot;<i>angels&quot;</i>. But <u>only if they're the same</u>, if the ST decides that you need other than Spirit to summon them, because aliens aren't spirits, you will complain. It ends transforming in the &quot;I do whatever I want&quot; Paradigm.<br /> I think that it's better if a character has a determined flavor, and tries to constrain it's workings to that flavor, even if it's slightly disadventageous. I accept that the player knows more about the character's paradigm than I do, but when you start streching the concept, it starts becoming harder and harder to buy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why are there rules in the books for doing exactly that? The fact that you can (at great penalty) overcome your restrictions on &quot;how&quot; through will illustrates that the game completely encourages role-playing mages as the kind of people that would consider doing it when desperate. If the book says, &quot;if you're denied your 'how' you can still try magic,&quot; it's pretty hard to justify the ST saying, &quot;no that's bad role-playing.&quot; The ST has mechanical penalties to lay down for characters knowingly acting at the edges of what their paradigm calls for.</div> </div> </div> </div>What rules?<br /> The rules that allow to use magick without an instrument that Technomancers can't use BECAUSE THEIR PARADIGM ABSOLUTELY FORBIDES THEM TO DO SO, BECAUSE THEY <u><i>BELIEVE </i></u>MAGICK IT'S EXTERNAL?<br /> <br /> Or the new rules that allow to use other mage's instruments, which contradict everything written in older books?<br /> <br /> You DO notice that they're contradictory and that you're just putting yourself in one side of that contradiction, don't you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, M20 actually addresses a lot of this in discussing paradigms (and specifically what sort of beliefs and structures make for successful paradigms). What you're calling &quot;overpowered&quot; it basically calls the default: most mages go for the most permissible paradigms in the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't prove that &quot;most mages go for the most permissible paradigms in the end&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> , because that would mean there are less technomancers than mystics in the world <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> , And that most mages are Chaos Mages, to choose instruments that aren't cumbersome <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (That's the mage you want to play?). NO mage chooses his paradigm because it's permisive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Paradigms aren't mean to be a &quot;check&quot; on character power, they're meant to be a framing device for your character's magic. The &quot;checks&quot; in the system are numerous and largely come in the form of consequences for your character's choices (which is, again, a major theme of the game) rather than limitations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, it's supposed to give flavor to the character. Do you think that you should choose a Paradigm based on how permissive it is?, Because that's what seems to be the case going for your previous statement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-18-2017, 02:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T11:41:06-08:00","id":1034139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1034131#post1034131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...]I think that it's better if a character has a determined flavor, and tries to constrain it's workings to that flavor, even if it's slightly disadventageous. I accept that the player knows more about the character's paradigm than I do, but when you start streching the concept, it starts becoming harder and harder to buy.[...]</div> </div> </div> </div>Very nicely worded.<br /> Sometimes I must remind me that it is a game and meant to be fun. If a PC wants to do what you think doesn't fit his Paradigm, then let it be. Use the Experience later to improve the depth of the Paradigm. As I often must remember myself: Prefer saying &quot;Yes&quot; over saying &quot;No&quot;, simply because it is more fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T12:00:24-08:00","id":1034152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1034131#post1034131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does your psychic believes he can summon angels...</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless you think that summoning angels is something you can do with the Mind Sphere, your response is a non sequitur. If the psychic has a mega-Cerebro that lets him use his powers at range and across dimensional barriers (AKA, he has Correspondence and Spirit and an appropriate focus for their use), then why CAN'T Professor X summon angels in the same way he'd have Wolverine come visit him in the Danger room if he didn't want to go all the way upstairs or use the household intercom to get him?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T12:07:25-08:00","id":1034160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1034131#post1034131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does your psychic believes he can summon angels?. If not, then he can't. Oh, but you're <i>very clever</i>, so you will summon <i>&quot;aliens&quot;</i>, not &quot;<i>angels&quot;</i>. But <u>only if they're the same</u>, if the ST decides that you need other than Spirit to summon them, because aliens aren't spirits, you will complain. It ends transforming in the &quot;I do whatever I want&quot; Paradigm.<br /> I think that it's better if a character has a determined flavor, and tries to constrain it's workings to that flavor, even if it's slightly disadventageous. I accept that the player knows more about the character's paradigm than I do, but when you start streching the concept, it starts becoming harder and harder to buy.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a psychic doesn't believe that he can summon angels - then he won't try to summon angels. This is what you are not getting - it is impossible for a character to try and do something that breaks their paradigm. Paradigm exists entirely in character's head, it's an internal, not external concept. You wouldn't try to do something that you know is impossible. If a psychic is trying to summon angels then he already accepted that it is possible for his psychic powers to produce angels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T12:29:15-08:00","id":1034167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you think that summoning angels is something you can do with the Mind Sphere, your response is a non sequitur. If the psychic has a mega-Cerebro that lets him use his powers at range and across dimensional barriers (AKA, he has Correspondence and Spirit and an appropriate focus for their use), then why CAN'T Professor X summon angels in the same way he'd have Wolverine come visit him in the Danger room if he didn't want to go all the way upstairs or use the household intercom to get him?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you're right that there may be a psychic that can &quot;summon angels&quot; (because he's a holy psychic that tries to understand the mind of God, or something like that). But you seem to disregard the opposite argument, that your psichic may not be so psychodelic. In fact, he probably won't (I've never seen such a thing, albeit I wouldn't necessarily oppose a paradigm like that). And that isn't wrong. It isn't wrong to choose a paradigm with limitations, almost all paradigms have them, and when they have them you can bet that there are thing your mage can't do even if the Spheres would let you...at least until he figures how to (which might require time, training, and maybe even some good old Paradigm Shift)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a psychic doesn't believe that he can summon angels - then he won't try to summon angels. This is what you are not getting - it is impossible for a character to try and do something that breaks their paradigm. Paradigm exists entirely in character's head, it's an internal, not external concept. You wouldn't try to do something that you know is impossible. If a psychic is trying to summon angels then he already accepted that it is possible for his psychic powers to produce angels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it is possible. You're not getting than a player can act out of character.<br /> <br /> An example (I wasn't the ST). A player was a Dreamspeaker that used feathers as a focus. In his mind, his magick worked trough making elaborate artwork using feathers to appraise the spirits. However, when in action, all that flavor devolved into moving some feathers in the air to cast firebals in the spot, because he was in a pinch. The player stated afterwards that this wasn't what he had in mind when building the character, and he was somewhat frustrated because of this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T12:49:19-08:00","id":1034181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1034167#post1034167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And that isn't wrong. It isn't wrong to choose a paradigm with limitations</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, it's not wrong to play a paradigm with limitations.<br /> <br /> It's also not wrong to play a paradigm without limitations....unless your stated or unstated goal is &quot;limit the applications of Sphere effects the players in my game can achieve.&quot; Which I don't agree with as a goal. tbh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T12:53:41-08:00","id":1034187,"title":"","content":"Unless an ST wants ubermunchkingamer, they should probably work out ahead of time with players want the limits of their paradigm are and keep them to it. In the Dresden Files, there are dozens of limitations to Harry's Paradign, and he is considered to be one of the top wizards in the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T12:59:12-08:00","id":1034192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1034167#post1034167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An example (I wasn't the ST). A player was a Dreamspeaker that used feathers as a focus. In his mind, his magick worked trough making elaborate artwork using feathers to appraise the spirits. However, when in action, all that flavor devolved into moving some feathers in the air to cast firebals in the spot, because he was in a pinch. The player stated afterwards that this wasn't what he had in mind when building the character, and he was somewhat frustrated because of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like an entirely different problem than the one discussed. The player imagined his character doing occult rituals, an idea which was crushed by reality of Mage spellcasting primarily taking seconds rather than hours or days. And honestly, yes, this is a real problem. All of the stuff about Virtual Adepts re-coding reality or Ecstatics using transcendent drugs becomes bullshit when spellcasting works on a combat time scale. But it's not a problem of paradigm limitations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T13:00:21-08:00","id":1034193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1034187#post1034187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless an ST wants ubermunchkingamer, they should probably work out ahead of time with players want the limits of their paradigm are and keep them to it. In the Dresden Files, there are dozens of limitations to Harry's Paradign, and he is considered to be one of the top wizards in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I brought up the Dresden Files because you seemed to poo-poo the idea of Mages using MagiCK to accomplish mundane things, like lighting candles. Not to discuss a paradigm without limitations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T13:30:19-08:00","id":1034212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1034192#post1034192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like an entirely different problem than the one discussed. The player imagined his character doing occult rituals, an idea which was crushed by reality of Mage spellcasting primarily taking seconds rather than hours or days. And honestly, yes, this is a real problem. All of the stuff about Virtual Adepts re-coding reality or Ecstatics using transcendent drugs becomes bullshit when spellcasting works on a combat time scale. But it's not a problem of paradigm limitations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it is a problem if the ST does not require supporting ritual behavior off screen as part of the Paradigm. For example, I usually require my Mage characters to spend one hour per level of Arete per day in supporting ritual activity as part of their Paradigm. If they do not do enough, they suffer a +3 difficulty for using the unsupported Arete (and have to spend one point of Willpower). Of course, the exact nature of the supporting ritual activity depends of their Paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T13:37:41-08:00","id":1034215,"title":"","content":"Mage is a game about being able to make anything true. To limit it is pointless, and you'll find your players too powerful sooner or later, unless you change the game to something else entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T14:30:12-08:00","id":1034247,"title":"","content":"No, I disagree, Changeling is the game about making anything come true, and it can be a much more balanced game than Mage. Mage tends to devolve into games of ubermunchkingamer if the ST does not clarify their positions on Paradigm and Paradox at the beginning of the chronicle. If players do not like the clarifications, then they can always not join the chronicle that the ST is running.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T14:49:01-08:00","id":1034257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1034131#post1034131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or maybe Timmy it's acting out of character, because his player it's metagaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, yet again, this is turning into less, &quot;what are the books actually getting at,&quot; and more, &quot;this game doesn't work well with an antagonistic relationship between the ST and the players.&quot;<br /> <br /> Being worried about players metagaming to cast stuff you as the ST don't think is a great fit for their paradigm is already approaching things the wrong way for the game. That's something we should be 100% in support of players trying, because that sort of shit brings out the consequences of why it's a bad idea in-universe (which is, again, a major theme of the game).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But <u>only if they're the same</u>, if the ST decides that you need other than Spirit to summon them, because aliens aren't spirits, you will complain. </div> </div> </div>This is Mage, one of the core design premises of Mage is that different paradigms all use the same rules. That's the only point. Shamans, reality hackers, and grand wizards all running the same rules despite their radically different magic.<br /> <br /> Also, Spirit is not the only way to contact or interact with Umbral entities (regardless of what you call them). Mind (though requiring higher levels and carrying some other risks) is capable of this on its own (since we shifting to the &quot;psychic superpowers&quot; example thing).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that it's better if a character has a determined flavor, and tries to constrain it's workings to that flavor, even if it's slightly disadventageous. </div> </div> </div>Great! M20 added lots of optional rules dials for this. Problem solved... right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The rules that allow to use magick without an instrument that Technomancers can't use BECAUSE THEIR PARADIGM ABSOLUTELY FORBIDES THEM TO DO SO, BECAUSE THEY <u><i>BELIEVE </i></u>MAGICK IT'S EXTERNAL? </div> </div> </div>Technocrats, not Technomancers. Technomancers are just locked out of it until higher Arete. And for Technocrats it's explicitly not their paradigm, but the social conditioning done by the Technocracy that's designed to stop them from realizing what non-Technocrat Technomancers will eventually realize and be able to pull off this trick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You DO notice that they're contradictory and that you're just putting yourself in one side of that contradiction, don't you? </div> </div> </div>I don't accept that the changes between editions truly impacts the point I'm making. Regardless of which edition we want to use, the games have always included ways for mages to overcome their paradigms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can't prove that &quot;most mages go for the most permissible paradigms in the end&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> , because that would mean there are less technomancers than mystics in the world <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> , </div> </div> </div>That logic doesn't work, because &quot;can use the trick to work without instruments before you're ready,&quot; is not the sole factor. Technomancers have high degrees of permissible actions when it comes to coincidental magic and working withing the modern world (aka having instruments at hand in almost every store in a developed area of the world) compared to mystic paradigms, which easily explains the popularity they enjoy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you think that you should choose a Paradigm based on how permissive it is?, Because that's what seems to be the case going for your previous statement. </div> </div> </div>No, I believe the the common paradigms presented in M20 are already of roughly equal permissible status and any custom paradigm should be equal to them. That's sort of the whole point the book is making there. Paradigms should be pretty permissible by default.<br /> <br /> If I feel like playing a more limited character on a mechanical level of impact... Revised has lots and lots of Flaws that are designed specifically around more restrictive than default paradigms to pull from until M20 gets a bigger list of those out. &quot;My character has too use blood no matter what,&quot; is supposed to be so above average in limitation, that it's worthy of Flaw bonuses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1034167#post1034167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're not getting than a player can act out of character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Harping on &quot;bad players&quot; doesn't have anything to do with this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1034187#post1034187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless an ST wants ubermunchkingamer,...</div> </div> </div> </div>Odd, I don't have any problems with those despite my supposedly super abuseable and hyper-lax approach to paradigms... maybe paradigm isn't actually the issue here...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1034212#post1034212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it is a problem if the ST does not require supporting ritual behavior off screen as part of the Paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no need to &quot;require&quot; this. It should be assumed to be happening off screen without the ST setting house rules to punish players for not specifying it. We don't penalize players for not explicitly spending enough time doing strength training in downtime so their effective Strength and Athletics are lowered or what not.<br /> <br /> This is a RPG, not a Sims management game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T14:49:22-08:00","id":1034259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1034247#post1034247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I disagree, Changeling is the game about making anything come true, and it can be a much more balanced game than Mage. Mage tends to devolve into games of ubermunchkingamer if the ST does not clarify their positions on Paradigm and Paradox at the beginning of the chronicle. If players do not like the clarifications, then they can always not join the chronicle that the ST is running.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;My way or the highway&quot; STs are as much, if not a bigger, problem than munchkining players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T22:54:40-08:00","id":1034468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1034259#post1034259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &amp;quot;My way or the highway&amp;quot; STs are as much, if not a bigger, problem than munchkining players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only as much, because a ST is a rare species.<br /> <br /> I had good experiences with foregoing XP costs for raising Arete.<br /> That way you have control of the Powerlevel. The Seeking is more meaningful and they can't complain because they save big numbers of XP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T14:42:15-08:00","id":1036285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1032271-managing-paradigm?p=1034247#post1034247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I disagree, Changeling is the game about making anything come true, and it can be a much more balanced game than Mage. Mage tends to devolve into games of ubermunchkingamer if the ST does not clarify their positions on Paradigm and Paradox at the beginning of the chronicle. If players do not like the clarifications, then they can always not join the chronicle that the ST is running.</div> </div> </div> </div>Roughly speaking, changeling is about going over the top. It had nothing directly to do with making everything possible. <br /> <br /> Mage is about will over matter, it's a game about player's agency, it's about the character believing in something higher than reality, and making reality fit to what they believe. You can see it by yourself: you are creating house rules to control it. <br /> <br /> As you said yourself, your players go munchkin quite easily. Maybe that's because the game was meant for this. No one here is saying that Mage don't have this level of power. What I am saying, and some other people too, is that the game was meant for playing with Unbound power. <br /> <br /> You choose it yourself: either you roll with the game as it is, and accept that the game is about not having many limits for the characters, or you deny it and continue creating rules over rules to correct what isn't wrong, and limit your munchkin players from being Mages. <br /> <br /> <br /> As a side note, i'm getting used to a converter from speech to text because of a quite painful crisis of tendonitis. So sorry if the text isn't very well written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T14:55:08-08:00","id":1036289,"title":"","content":"I never actually had to limit my players. Between the rules for Paradigm, Pattern Bleeding, Paradox, etc the rules were able to limit them for me. Of course, that never stopped my players from trying to convince me that the rules did not apply to them.<br /> <br /> If STs are willing to enforce the rules, then Mage is manageable. If you want to do an effect outside of the Paradigm, you suffer the same penalties as if you were trying to circumvent foci. If you want lasting effects, you suffer Pattern Bleed. If you want lasting supernatural Attributes, you suffer Permanent Paradox. If you try anything vulgar, you suffer Paradox. If you want to turn the air to silver to kill a Garou, it is an Outlandish Feat and requires ten successes. The solutions are in the rules, people just ignore them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T15:16:39-08:00","id":1036298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want to do an effect outside of the Paradigm, you suffer the same penalties as if you were trying to circumvent foci. </div> </div> </div> As per M20, if you want to do an effect outside of the Paradigm (not the way it's worded in the book, they word it as &quot;using unfamiliar tools&quot;) you get a +2 to difficulty, and the spell it's Vulgar with Witnesses (you're the witness). If you try to circumvent foci, on the other hand, it's a +3 to difficulty, and you need to spend a Willpower point, the spell it's likely to become be Vulgar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-22-2017, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T15:33:35-08:00","id":1036305,"title":"","content":"Interesting change and, depending on the effect, it may be worse than circumventing foci, though not for vulgar effects in front of witnesses. Lightning bolts become difficulty 9 (-1 success) and, with Forces 3, that means life sucks for the Mage because you are doing very little damage for the Paradox you are gaining.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}